a":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f97e87e9806222e48","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"'Where it comes from' / 'The fix direction' section and Acceptance criteria","norm_id":"n3c4a5b0185e58aa3","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future engineer hits a third ceiling-like symptom and needs to understand why the fetch partitions the way it does and what the seam invariants are"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add an acceptance criterion that the selected partition strategy and its seam invariants are documented (ADR or a docstring block in fetch_paging.py) alongside the implementation.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2857,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the failure-disposition contract for the partitioned fetch's seam: when any single slice fails (or trips a preserved stall guard) after earlier slices succeeded, declare that the whole pass fails atomically with a single retryable disposition and that NO partial/accumulated union is ever handed to `_build_snapshot`.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["project.failure-disposition-contract"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.801,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'slice by status, by updated-date window, or by key range, and union the results'","Plan: guards 'each still raise or continue as they do today, proven by tests at the seam between slices'","ABSENCE: the plan states the guards must still RAISE at the seam, but does not state what disposition (retryable/transient vs fatal — discard-partial-and-fail vs surface-partial) the caller sees when one slice of an N-slice union fails after others succeeded"],"finding":"Partitioning the fetch into slices and unioning the results introduces a new composite failure arm — a per-slice fetch that fails (or a slice that raises one of the preserved stall guards) AFTER earlier slices have already succeeded and been accumulated. The plan requires the existing guards to 'still raise or continue as they do today' at the seam, but it never states the DISPOSITION the caller surfaces when a slice fails mid-union: is a partial union discarded and the whole pass surfaced as a single retryable failure, or could a partial/incomplete snapshot escape? Stating this per-arm disposition prevents a partitioned-fetch failure from silently degrading to an under-populated snapshot — the exact class of bug the ceiling guard exists to prevent.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f61c343a20e619812","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"'Why raising the constant is the WRONG fix' (partition direction) and AC: 'The existing anti-truncation guarantees still hold across the new partition seam'","norm_id":"nae7b24b3eefb50d2","priority":0.099,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Slice 3 of 5 hits a cursor-stall after slices 1-2 accumulated: without a stated disposition, an implementation might return the partial union (a truncated snapshot — the guarded-against bug) instead of failing the whole pass as one loud, retryable failure"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add an inline contract, e.g.: 'a per-slice failure aborts the whole pass and surfaces as one retryable failure (same disposition as today's SilentTruncationError); the partially-accumulated union is discarded, never returned — so no truncated snapshot can escape at the seam.'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Name the immutable `created` window as the chosen partition dimension and explicitly warn off `updated` (mutable — mid-pass touches migrate across the boundary) and key-range (silent-drop at deleted/moved-key gaps), rather than listing all three as interchangeable options.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.734,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'partition the query ... slice by status, by updated-date window, or by key range, and union the results'","fetch_paging.py:207-224 documents WHY created and NOT issuekey (gap slots) and WHY not updated (mutable, migrates across the boundary mid-pass)","The plan requires preserving anti-truncation guarantees but a key-range/updated partition can drop whole issues at the seam, which those guarantees do not catch"],"finding":"The plan's fix-direction sentence presents three slice dimensions as a co-equal menu ('slice by status, by updated-date window, or by key range') but two of them are silent-drop traps for this problem: a key-range partition drops issues at the ~1000 gap slots left by deleted/moved keys (a 500-wide tiling summed 979 against a true ~1388), and an 'updated'-date window is mutable so an issue touched mid-pass migrates across the boundary and is missed by both windows. Only an immutable 'created' window partitions the space complementarily for any instant. Offering the trap dimensions without flagging them invites the implementer to pick a partition key that reintroduces exactly the silent-partial defect this module exists to refuse.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f049d78f008ba7531","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan section 'Why raising the constant is the WRONG fix' — the fix-direction sentence","norm_id":"n2ca8cff96b37ec5b","priority":0.066,"reason":"veto:plan-goal-satisfied","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer selects key-range tiling and loses issues at deleted-key gaps with no error raised","Implementer selects updated-window and an issue re-touched during the pass falls between two slices"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Replace the menu with a single recommended dimension plus its rationale, e.g. 'Partition by the IMMUTABLE `created` field into half-open windows: created is stable across the pass and `created < X` / `created >= X` partition the space complementarily for any instant X. Do NOT partition by `updated` (an issue touched mid-pass migrates across the boundary and is missed by both windows) or by key range (deleted/moved keys leave gaps, so a key-width slice silently under-counts).'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"yes","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v5","material_fingerprint":"47037dad01bb775c","material_parts":{"children":["647ea2107ca5072f",0],"description":["7725955236592551",4397],"description_boxes":["b7fb217694ae2d30",6],"file_impact":["b0c676692ac09edd",3],"ticket_id":["264465fe715cbd25",19]},"metrics":{"cache_read_tokens":440815,"cache_write_tokens":164432,"claim_path":"no-llm/no-network (structural; the fast claim check is a local HMAC verify)","det_ms":19182.0,"input_tokens":627006,"llm_calls":29,"llm_ms":220147.3,"output_tokens":21391,"precheck":{"cited_anchor_warning":false},"total_ms":286579.5,"verify_requests":5},"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6","priority_floor":0.8,"provider_provenance":{"candidates":["bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6","anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-6"],"capabilities":{"native_structured_output":true,"prompt_cache_style":"bedrock","supports_temperature":true,"supports_thinking":true,"web_access":"off"},"endpoint_host":null,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6","provider":"bedrock","ran_model":"bedrock:us.anthropi